1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:02,793
Stand in the oldest known ochre mine
in the world.

2
00:00:03,193 --> 00:00:04,620
It is called Lion Cavern.

3
00:00:04,640 --> 00:00:08,227
Ngwenya means crocodile, named for a
mountain shaped like one.

4
00:00:08,627 --> 00:00:11,847
Researchers dated the digging to about
forty-eight thousand years ago.

5
00:00:12,247 --> 00:00:17,525
Ochre makes a red pigment, so these first
miners were already reshaping their world.

6
00:00:17,925 --> 00:00:21,810
A ranger walks you up an easy trail and a
steel staircase to the cave.

7
00:00:21,830 --> 00:00:24,396
The view over the old mine is worth the
climb.

8
00:00:24,796 --> 00:00:27,858
The site is on the tentative list for
UNESCO World Heritage status.

